e-wir-begehren-carolin-emcke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Gay youth","sourceId":"source-open-library-wie-wir-begehren-carolin-emcke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Psychology","sourceId":"source-open-library-wie-wir-begehren-carolin-emcke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Desire","sourceId":"source-open-library-wie-wir-begehren-carolin-emcke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Male homosexuality","sourceId":"source-open-library-wie-wir-begehren-carolin-emcke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Masculinity","sourceId":"source-open-library-wie-wir-begehren-carolin-emcke"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Societies","sourceId":"source-open-library-wie-wir-begehren-carolin-emcke"}],"publicationYear":2012,"pageCount":253,"summary":"What if, instead of discovering our sexuality only once, during puberty, we discover it again later--and then again, after that? What if our sexuality reinvents itself every time our desire shifts, every time the object of our desire changes? What if the nature of our desire is constantly changing--growing deeper, lighter, wilder, more reckless, more tender, more selfish, more devoted, more radical? How We Desire is an enthralling essay about gender, sexuality and love by one of Germany's most admired writers. It's about growing up, and discovering the contours of desire and difference, about understanding that we sometimes 'slip into norms the way we slip into clothes, putting them on because they're laid out ready for us'. In telling her own story, Emcke draws back the veil on how we experience desire, no matter what our sexual orientation.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8537761-L.jpg","experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Sexuality continually re